From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: map the speaker
 ports statically

Without qcom,port-mapping, the SoundWire controller hands out its ports in
order to whatever amplifier ports are enabled. Its ports are laid out for
left DAC, COMP, BOOST, right DAC, COMP, BOOST, then the two VI sense inputs,
so any switch setting other than DAC, COMP and BOOST on and VISENSE off moves
the following ports onto the wrong controller ports: with BOOST off and
VISENSE on, VI sense data lands in output slots and the amplifiers report bus
clashes at high levels; with both off, the right DAC gets port 3 and the right
speaker stays silent.

Map the amplifier ports to their controller ports.

The right amplifier's VI sense input lands on port 8, the last port of the
controller, which qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports() can hand out only with
"soundwire: qcom: let the last data port be allocated"; without it a
stream with VI sense enabled fails with "All ports busy".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index b88dfce0a..e5be4f8f5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1288,6 +1288,7 @@ left_spkr: wsa8830-left@0,1 {
 		sound-name-prefix = "SpkrLeft";
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 		vdd-supply = <&vreg_s10b>;
+		qcom,port-mapping = <1 2 3 7>;
 	};
 
 	right_spkr: wsa8830-right@0,2 {
@@ -1300,6 +1301,7 @@ right_spkr: wsa8830-right@0,2 {
 		sound-name-prefix = "SpkrRight";
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 		vdd-supply = <&vreg_s10b>;
+		qcom,port-mapping = <4 5 6 8>;
 	};
 };
 
